1	//! End-to-end regression tests for
2	//! `roottrace verify <record-file> <proof-file> <trusted-tree-size> <trusted-root>`.
3	//!
4	//! The fixed proof vectors are the SAME independently produced constants used
5	//! by `prove_regression.rs` (generated by
6	//! `tests/reference/rfc6962_vectors.py`, which computes RFC 6962 audit paths
7	//! two structurally different ways and re-verifies them with `hashlib`); they
8	//! are never derived from roottrace output. Where a proof is needed for a
9	//! position without a fixed constant, the test runs `roottrace prove` and
10	//! feeds its output straight to `roottrace verify`, covering interop with the
11	//! existing command byte for byte.
12	//!
13	//! Coverage:
14	//!   * success: stdout is exactly "verified\n", exit 0, stderr empty
15	//!   * compact, pretty and field-reordered proof JSON all verify
16	//!   * the record file is taken verbatim: empty file = empty record, while a
17	//!     trailing LF/space/CR, NUL and non-UTF-8 differences change the record
18	//!   * the trusted size and root come ONLY from the command line and must
19	//!     match the proof; the proof's own fields cannot substitute
20	//!   * duplicate content is checked at the declared leaf_index only
21	//!   * short/long audit paths (incl. a non-empty path for a one-record tree)
22	//!     fail
23	//!   * malformed proofs exit 1 with an "invalid proof" message and no stdout
24	//!   * argument errors exit 2 with usage; read failures exit 1
25	
26	mod common;
27	
28	use std::process::Command;
29	
30	use common::{TempDir, TempFile};
